WEBVTT

00:08.370 --> 00:12.110
District 4 and 5, keep up your bombardment!

00:12.110 --> 00:13.110
<i>Roger!</i>

00:14.220 --> 00:19.060
I frequent that super market 
shooting beams right now...

00:19.060 --> 00:23.500
This just shows you Ratatoskr's facilities 
extend well beyond the underground.

00:23.990 --> 00:27.090
All ships! Commence fire 
on the enemy battleships!

00:27.090 --> 00:29.500
Wizard Team, support our Spirits!

00:29.500 --> 00:30.500
<i>Roger!</i>

00:35.510 --> 00:37.270
Gabriel!

00:37.270 --> 00:38.480
Haniel!

00:38.480 --> 00:40.010
Kaleidoscope!

00:45.590 --> 00:50.530
So this is Gabriel? 
I do feel like it's grown stronger.

00:50.530 --> 00:51.250
Yes!

00:51.250 --> 00:53.570
Now to just scatter our foes!

02:29.500 --> 02:32.550
So thrilling, so thrilling!

02:33.920 --> 02:38.170
To think they would try 
to stop me with such forces!

02:38.170 --> 02:40.490
They sure are underestimating me.

02:47.070 --> 02:50.350
Hmph, here come the mass-produced models.

02:50.350 --> 02:52.220
Mass-produced models?

02:52.220 --> 02:55.210
You're the one person 
I don't want to hear that from.

02:55.210 --> 02:57.170
I've thought this for a while,

02:57.170 --> 03:00.490
but your character overlaps 
with ours, doesn't it?

03:00.770 --> 03:02.500
Bring it on.

03:02.500 --> 03:08.250
I'll lay out your heads 
before your beloved "Father".

03:19.940 --> 03:22.130
What is this?

03:22.130 --> 03:27.470
Captain, this is what Origami 
was trying to tell us about, isn't it?

03:27.980 --> 03:29.270
Looks like it.

03:29.780 --> 03:33.770
This isn't a fight against Spirits anymore.

03:34.870 --> 03:38.420
<i>Hello, captain of the JGSDF's AST.</i>

03:38.780 --> 03:43.060
<i>This is Irene Fox from DEM's 
Second Executive Branch.</i>

03:43.460 --> 03:44.660
DEM?

03:44.660 --> 03:46.290
<i>Cutting to the point,</i>

03:46.290 --> 03:50.060
<i>please follow our orders 
and charge the Spirits.</i>

03:50.060 --> 03:51.610
<i>We'll provide cover.</i>

03:51.610 --> 03:54.240
Huh? What's the big idea?

03:54.240 --> 03:57.850
<i>You all are at least capable of that, right?</i>

03:57.850 --> 03:58.790
<i>Later.</i>

04:02.170 --> 04:05.870
Captain, are we going to follow DEM's orders?

04:07.640 --> 04:11.660
If there's a Spirit before us, 
it's our job to defeat them,

04:12.500 --> 04:14.650
regardless of DEM's orders.

04:15.100 --> 04:16.310
Let's go!

04:22.770 --> 04:24.400
Be careful of that chill!

04:24.400 --> 04:26.610
It'll freeze you and your Territory!

04:26.610 --> 04:27.490
Roger!

04:33.750 --> 04:34.620
Wha?!

04:34.620 --> 04:36.540
Michael, Lataib!

04:43.630 --> 04:44.530
Huh?

04:48.650 --> 04:54.980
Hmm, are you all the AST 
that Origami mentioned?

04:54.980 --> 04:58.840
Y-You're a Spirit, right?

04:58.840 --> 05:01.430
You saved us?

05:02.030 --> 05:05.480
They were intending to use you all as decoys.

05:05.480 --> 05:06.910
Don't fall for it.

05:08.960 --> 05:11.860
We heard about you from Origami,

05:11.860 --> 05:14.140
so please get away from here.

05:15.430 --> 05:17.780
C-Captain, are you hurt?

05:17.780 --> 05:18.820
I'm fine.

05:18.820 --> 05:20.530
Thanks to that woman.

05:22.910 --> 05:24.100
All of you!

05:24.530 --> 05:26.830
Start preparing to look for another job!

05:35.410 --> 05:36.730
Artemisia.

05:36.730 --> 05:37.850
Long time, no see.

05:37.850 --> 05:42.110
It's Origami Tobiichi, right?

05:42.820 --> 05:45.220
Seeing you gives me the creeps.

05:47.330 --> 05:49.780
Have we met somewhere before?

05:50.080 --> 05:53.660
You've had your memories manipulated by DEM.

05:53.660 --> 05:54.350
Huh?

05:56.070 --> 05:58.670
It's possible for us to cure you of that.

05:59.130 --> 06:00.380
Are you suggesting

06:00.750 --> 06:04.880
that Westcott is deceiving me?

06:05.210 --> 06:06.020
Yes.

06:07.940 --> 06:10.590
Sorry, but I can't believe you.

06:11.010 --> 06:13.890
After all, you're Spirits.

06:19.690 --> 06:24.310
Whoa, I'm the one you'll be facing!

06:25.440 --> 06:26.440
Yoshinon!

06:26.440 --> 06:27.580
Here I go!

06:27.580 --> 06:30.200
Bad girls get frozen!

06:36.200 --> 06:37.160
Metatron!

06:47.990 --> 06:49.720
You're quite good.

06:50.660 --> 06:51.850
<i>Oririn!</i>

06:51.850 --> 06:53.720
<i>This a little bad news,</i>

06:53.720 --> 06:55.850
<i>but Ellen is heading your way!</i>

07:01.540 --> 07:03.610
You came, Ellen?

07:03.940 --> 07:05.730
Wise judgment.

07:06.010 --> 07:07.570
You've matured.

07:09.220 --> 07:10.140
Karen.

07:15.370 --> 07:16.790
Please handle the rest.

07:25.070 --> 07:26.140
Elliot.

07:27.130 --> 07:31.910
May I tell a joke to help 
calm tensions in the room?

07:32.900 --> 07:33.890
Oh?

07:35.730 --> 07:38.010
Let's run, Elliot.

07:38.010 --> 07:42.020
Leave behind Ratatoskr, 
the Spirits, everything.

07:44.970 --> 07:48.450
We can go live somewhere 
together, just the two of us.

07:49.330 --> 07:51.780
I would like at least three kids.

07:51.780 --> 07:52.780
Karen.

07:55.140 --> 07:57.280
That was my best joke.

07:59.030 --> 08:01.910
Yeah, you have talent as comedian.

08:18.200 --> 08:20.940
Origami Tobiichi and Mana Takamiya...

08:21.380 --> 08:24.940
Perfect. I'll eliminate you both together.

08:28.450 --> 08:29.400
Who goes there?!

08:34.620 --> 08:37.410
Hey. Long time, no see, Ellen.

08:37.790 --> 08:42.290
Did you have fun acting like you're 
the strongest in a world without me?

08:42.610 --> 08:45.670
Elliot!

08:49.710 --> 08:52.380
This is lame.

08:52.380 --> 08:57.620
Right? I can't believe we're being assigned 
the boring work of assaulting cannons.

08:57.620 --> 08:59.180
Oh, look, look.

09:00.810 --> 09:03.180
Looks like this might get a little interesting.

09:04.460 --> 09:06.900
Beelzebub Yeled!

09:16.210 --> 09:17.610
So weak!

09:17.610 --> 09:23.080
I wanted to play a bit more, but Father 
will get mad if we take too long.

09:23.370 --> 09:26.580
You're finished!

09:34.890 --> 09:37.130
Leave this place to us!

09:37.130 --> 09:39.470
Evacuate. Please fall back.

09:39.800 --> 09:41.410
Th-Thanks...

09:42.250 --> 09:44.600
Are you serious?

09:45.090 --> 09:47.010
Princess and Berserk!

09:47.010 --> 09:49.090
The fighters are all here!

09:49.550 --> 09:53.480
Do you think you can beat us with numbers?

09:53.890 --> 09:57.600
With me, one is all, and all are one.

09:57.600 --> 10:01.600
No matter how many of us you kill, 
we won't die as long as Beelzebub exists.

10:01.600 --> 10:04.080
How do you hope to kill a woman who can't die?

10:04.420 --> 10:08.830
Sorry, Nibeelcole, but we're not your opponent.

10:09.790 --> 10:13.020
We have someone much better 
suited to facing you!

10:13.020 --> 10:16.720
Affirmative. We're simply their backup.

10:16.720 --> 10:18.010
Huh?

10:25.800 --> 10:26.490
Huh?

10:41.530 --> 10:44.050
Shido Itsuka?

10:44.500 --> 10:47.410
Wow, that's awfully bold, isn't it?

10:47.720 --> 10:49.860
You are our opponent?

10:50.900 --> 10:52.370
Are you underestimating us?

10:52.370 --> 10:56.420
If I kill you, then it means 
my father has won this battle.

10:56.420 --> 10:58.090
Are you stupid?

10:58.090 --> 11:00.680
Now I'll have a great present for Father!

11:13.870 --> 11:16.070
Nibeelcole, I love you.

11:16.070 --> 11:17.070
Huh?

11:21.950 --> 11:23.070
Huh?

11:35.910 --> 11:37.590
What's going on?!

11:37.880 --> 11:40.490
Nibeelcole eliminated! It worked!

11:41.160 --> 11:44.380
<i>Nibeelcole is still a Spirit, too.</i>

11:44.380 --> 11:48.220
<i>Which means Shido's power can seal her, as well.</i>

11:48.630 --> 11:51.500
<i>Nibeelcole originates from Beelzebub,</i>

11:51.500 --> 11:55.630
<i>but he didn't manage to steal 
the entirety of Nia's crystal.</i>

11:56.100 --> 12:00.970
Meaning I'm still influencing Little Rouge.

12:00.970 --> 12:06.780
So whether or not he can seal them 
depends on my affection for him.

12:06.780 --> 12:10.120
<i>Yes. This is a vulgar way of putting it,</i>

12:10.440 --> 12:15.630
<i>but they're loose girls whose bodies are 
honest no matter how much they say no.</i>

12:15.940 --> 12:16.990
Raphael!

12:20.760 --> 12:23.590
Now, let's begin, Nibeelcole.

12:23.590 --> 12:26.510
It's time for our date.

12:27.170 --> 12:29.040
Don't underestimate us!

12:42.020 --> 12:44.860
Then I just need to avoid getting close!

12:55.170 --> 12:57.420
Now, who's next?

12:58.420 --> 13:00.410
Father!

13:00.410 --> 13:02.590
I'm not letting you go, kittens.

13:12.490 --> 13:14.680
The impact's more impressive than I imagined.

13:14.680 --> 13:16.550
Way to go, Shido!

13:16.550 --> 13:19.830
I think this what they call unparalleled.

13:20.310 --> 13:24.350
Watchful. There seems to be 
no need for us to act.

13:25.460 --> 13:27.030
That's not the case. Here they come!

13:27.030 --> 13:28.770
We won't let you interfere!

13:28.770 --> 13:31.120
Shido, we leave the rest to you.

13:31.120 --> 13:32.760
You can count on me!

13:32.760 --> 13:34.120
Come on, come on.

13:35.380 --> 13:38.100
Give up already. It's no use running.

13:38.100 --> 13:39.540
Shido! Behind you!

13:49.450 --> 13:50.760
You're impressive.

13:51.170 --> 13:52.180
So are you.

13:52.550 --> 13:55.060
But you can't win just by running.

13:56.190 --> 13:58.270
I wonder what you're thinking?

14:02.150 --> 14:04.090
<i>Perfect timing.</i>

14:04.090 --> 14:09.430
<i>This is Artemisia Ashcroft with DEM's 
Second Executive Branch.</i>

14:09.430 --> 14:10.940
<i>I'm currently engaged with a Spirit.</i>

14:10.940 --> 14:12.090
<i>Lend assistance.</i>

14:12.090 --> 14:14.540
Sorry, but we can't meet your expectations.

14:14.810 --> 14:17.180
<i>After all, we're unemployed!</i>

14:27.720 --> 14:29.170
A draw?

14:29.170 --> 14:31.600
No, it's my win.

14:31.600 --> 14:32.410
No.

14:34.590 --> 14:36.220
It's our win.

14:37.280 --> 14:37.810
Huh?

14:38.450 --> 14:40.540
Michael, Lataib.

14:42.610 --> 14:45.250
Was I useful to you, Origami?

14:45.250 --> 14:46.140
Thank you.

14:46.660 --> 14:50.450
Ultimately our two-stage decoy strategy worked.

14:50.740 --> 14:53.740
Though I honestly intended 
to ask Mana to handle it.

14:54.380 --> 14:56.200
I'm sorry I was delayed!

14:56.200 --> 14:59.090
It took time for me to handle the Bandersnatch!

14:59.090 --> 15:00.210
Don't worry.

15:00.210 --> 15:02.890
You made the right decision, Captain.

15:02.890 --> 15:04.710
Don't give me that shit!

15:04.710 --> 15:08.230
Jeez, there's no going back for us now!

15:08.230 --> 15:11.720
Good bye to my life as a public servant.

15:14.250 --> 15:18.590
You're the real one, not a clone, right?

15:18.590 --> 15:22.240
Yes, I'm surprised you could tell.

15:22.240 --> 15:23.730
Kurumi, I...

15:32.900 --> 15:34.730
This is the battlefield.

15:34.730 --> 15:36.890
You mustn't let your guard down.

15:36.890 --> 15:39.470
Y-Yeah. Thank you.

15:39.950 --> 15:41.730
You saved my life.

15:43.730 --> 15:46.170
You're making an awfully big deal about it.

15:46.170 --> 15:47.850
I'm not just referring to now.

15:48.270 --> 15:51.950
I'm honestly grateful for 
all the times you've saved me so far.

15:52.530 --> 15:54.930
I really wanted to tell you that in person.

15:55.370 --> 15:58.260
My, my, why thank you.

15:58.670 --> 16:03.420
Then might I have your Spirit power 
as a show of appreciation?

16:03.420 --> 16:05.440
That's a different matter!

16:05.440 --> 16:07.770
That's unfortunate.

16:08.130 --> 16:11.780
Then I'll have to change my approach.

16:18.750 --> 16:20.950
Kurumi, I am grateful to you!

16:22.580 --> 16:23.780
But you know,

16:23.780 --> 16:30.460
I don't recall ever asking you to fight 
in my stead while I hide from DEM!

16:31.020 --> 16:35.090
I would never be happy if you saved me 
in exchange for your own life!

16:35.910 --> 16:38.220
You underestimate me, don't you?

16:38.220 --> 16:42.520
You just need to remain quietly on the ship.

16:42.520 --> 16:47.120
Then once the battle is over, 
you can greet me with tears of gratitude,

16:47.120 --> 16:50.570
and offer your Spirit power up to me!

16:51.130 --> 16:56.020
That just means I would 
die to you instead of DEM!

16:56.020 --> 16:58.740
I already told you, didn't I?

16:59.250 --> 17:05.000
I'll use your Spirit power to go to the past 
and defeat the Spirit of Origin!

17:05.790 --> 17:11.530
When you next come to, you'll be in 
a new world full of peace and happiness!

17:11.530 --> 17:13.560
You think it'll go that well?

17:13.560 --> 17:18.240
I don't want to hear that from the man 
who actually managed to alter the past!

17:18.240 --> 17:21.010
Now that you mention it, I did do that, damn it.

17:21.010 --> 17:22.720
Once I alter the past,

17:22.720 --> 17:29.220
the existence of Spirits 
and your death will be no more!

17:29.220 --> 17:30.870
What are you unsatisfied with about that?

17:31.400 --> 17:36.780
Then the very fact that you and I met 
would also be no more, now wouldn't it?!

17:37.280 --> 17:39.420
I love you!

17:39.420 --> 17:41.990
And I know you love me, too!

17:42.950 --> 17:45.570
Wh-What are you saying?!

17:45.570 --> 17:47.120
Don't forget!

17:47.120 --> 17:50.310
I've experienced your memories with Yod!

17:51.780 --> 17:53.950
I know how you feel!

17:55.170 --> 17:57.430
Even if that is true,

17:57.700 --> 18:03.830
saying that while you're kissing 
another woman is deplorable.

18:04.460 --> 18:07.060
I'm truly sorry about that!

18:09.230 --> 18:10.820
Kurumi, listen to me.

18:10.820 --> 18:13.640
Once this battle is over, 
I'll return to the past!

18:13.640 --> 18:14.440
Huh?

18:14.440 --> 18:18.420
I won't redo everything, only the bad parts!

18:18.420 --> 18:20.900
I'll seal the Spirit of Origin's power,

18:20.900 --> 18:23.700
and use that power to rewrite history!

18:23.700 --> 18:26.700
I'll make it so the misfortune 
that befell your friend, you,

18:26.700 --> 18:31.460
and all of the other Spirits never happened,

18:31.460 --> 18:35.590
and I'll ensure that I meet you 
and everyone else once again!

18:35.590 --> 18:41.210
I'll recreate the ultimate 
favorable and happy history!

18:41.210 --> 18:44.740
What are you...? Do you have any chance to...?

18:44.740 --> 18:46.750
You said it yourself, right?

18:48.090 --> 18:54.660
I'm the only the person in this world 
who has successfully rewritten history!

18:58.290 --> 19:02.950
Stop ignoring me 
and creating your own little world!

19:09.300 --> 19:10.490
Die!

19:10.490 --> 19:11.620
Kurumi, dodge!

19:23.250 --> 19:24.250
Dalet.

19:36.770 --> 19:38.060
Me!

19:43.510 --> 19:47.150
See? I proved useful, didn't I?

19:48.040 --> 19:49.530
Yes.

19:49.530 --> 19:53.920
I hate to admit it, 
you proved worth keeping alive.

19:55.220 --> 19:56.730
Please...

20:03.810 --> 20:09.300
Be honest with our own feelings.

20:28.540 --> 20:29.540
Kurumi.

20:31.040 --> 20:39.670
That clone was cocky, rebellious, 
meddlesome, and hopeless...

20:41.190 --> 20:44.850
but she finally proved useful before dying.

20:47.110 --> 20:52.690
Shido, do you remember our competition?

20:52.690 --> 20:54.540
Competition?

20:54.540 --> 20:56.630
Whoever makes the other fall for them wins?

20:59.420 --> 21:03.290
Let's continue our chat 
after this battle is over.

21:04.250 --> 21:07.150
Once we've driven away DEM...

21:07.770 --> 21:12.500
I wouldn't mind offering you my lips.

21:12.900 --> 21:14.770
You mean it, Kurumi?!

21:14.770 --> 21:18.860
That's only if we can defeat DEM.

21:20.130 --> 21:22.890
Can you do that, Shido?

21:23.380 --> 21:25.250
Of course I can!

21:25.250 --> 21:26.940
If I can't pull that off,

21:26.940 --> 21:29.640
then how could I face the Spirit of Origin?!

21:32.980 --> 21:33.780
Huh?

21:40.110 --> 21:41.150
What?!

21:52.740 --> 21:55.000
<b>Episode 3</b>

21:52.740 --> 21:55.000
<b>The Spirit's Resurrection</b>

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
Episode 4 "The Spirit of Origin"

23:25.750 --> 23:28.860
That is a memory of a distant past,

23:29.470 --> 23:31.770
and the tale of how Mio and Shinji met.

23:32.800 --> 23:36.180
Next Episode is Episode 4: 
The Spirit of Origin.

23:36.740 --> 23:39.330
I'll never let go of you again.
